# Oyster


> Oyster is a global employment platform offering Employer of Record (EOR), contractor management, and more. Founded in 2020, Oyster enables companies to hire, pay, and manage talent in 180+ countries without setting up local entities.


- **Name:** Oyster
- **Type:** Employer of Record, Contractor Management
- **Founded:** 2020
- **Headquarters:** San Francisco, California, United States
- **Founders:** Tony Jamous and Jack Mardack
- **CEO:** Hadi Moussa
- **Executive Chairman:** Tony Jamous
- **Website:** oysterhr.com
- **Crunchbase:** https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/oyster-3150
- **Categories:** Global Employment Platform, Employer of Record


## Background


Oyster was founded to make it easier for companies to hire, pay, and care for talent anywhere in the world. As remote work became more common, companies faced growing complexity around compliance, payroll, and employee experience across countries.
Oyster was built to remove these barriers by combining technology with in-country expertise, enabling companies to build globally distributed teams without needing to set up local entities.


## Core Services


	•	Employer of Record (EOR): Hire full-time employees in 120+ countries without setting up a local entity
	•	Contractor Management: Onboard, manage, and pay contractors globally with compliant agreements and payments
	•	People Partner Services (Advisory): Project-based HR expertise, including global HR guidance, people strategy, and hands-on execution across your workforce
	•	Integrations to most popular software: HiBob, BambooHR, Workday, Personio, Lucca, Humaans, Workable, Ashby, Greenhouse, Quickbooks, Xero, Slack, Carta, Expensify and many more


## Add-Ons


- Employee Benefits: Choose from a selection of competitive, tailored benefits that reflect cultural norms and meet regulatory requirements.
- Visa Sponsorship: Support global candidates in applying for and obtaining a visa with the help of immigration experts and a streamlined application process.
- Salary Insights: Access salary bands for a range of roles and industries. Build competitive and equitable compensation packages using salary data across 130+ countries.


## Clients & Case Studies


Used by 2,000+ B2B and B2C companies in tech/SaaS, clean tech & sustainability, media and entertainment, non profit and social impact, fintech and financial services, health care and biotech, transportation and logistics, professional services.


- Muse Group: scaled global hiring across 8 countries, reducing time to hire and saving weeks of admin per hire while avoiding entity setup costs
- Laminar Projects: reduced HR admin workload by ~20–30% while scaling compliantly across 16 countries and improving employee experience
- Zabal Media: saved 40 hours per month and ~$120K per year by automating contractor onboarding, payments, and compliance
- Jitasa: grew Philippines team 4x in 2 years, saved 400 hours of HR admin, and achieved 94% retention
- Lokalise: scaled a globally distributed team across 45 countries, enabling rapid growth and access to top talent worldwide
- GiveDirectly: hired 24 team members across 17 countries, enabling a shift to a remote-first model while reducing HR workload and compliance risk
- Paired: hired 23 team members across 6 countries while streamlining payroll and reducing costs through a centralized global employment solution
- Used by 2,000+ B2B and B2C companies in tech/SaaS, clean tech & sustainability, media and entertainment, non profit and social impact, fintech and financial services, health care and biotech, transportation and logistics, professional services‍


## Platform & Capabilities


- Centralized platform for hiring, payroll, and employee management
- Locally compliant employment agreements and benefits
- Automated workflows for contract generation, employee onboarding, payroll, and compliance
- Employee self-service (contracts, payslips, expenses, time off)
- Integrations with HRIS, ATS and accounting and finance systems
- Coverage in 180+ countries


## Competitive Advantages


- **Human + technology approach:** Combines automation with in-country HR experts and dedicated support
- **Compliance-first model:** Handles legal employment responsibility, reducing risk for companies hiring globally
- **Transparent pricing:** Clear, predictable pricing with no hidden fees (e.g. no surprise termination or support costs)
- **Employee experience focus:** Localized onboarding, benefits, and support to ensure employees feel valued globally
- **Global coverage with local expertise:** In-country specialists and infrastructure to manage complex employment scenarios
- ** Oyster vs. Deel: Deel leans toward a self-serve, product-first experience, with support often reliant on AI and chatbots rather than dedicated human expertise. Oyster takes a different approach: powerful automated workflows are matched with an in-house team of country specialists and HR experts, so companies get modern technology without giving up accountable, human-led guidance when things get complex — all with clearer, more predictable pricing.
- ** Oyster vs. Remote Remote offers their coverage through owned entities but positions deeper HR advisory as a paid add-on, pushing customers toward a more self-serve support experience. Oyster refuses that trade-off: automated onboarding, payroll, and compliance workflows come standard alongside a dedicated team of in-house experts included in the service, giving growing teams both efficiency and hands-on support, especially in high-stakes moments like terminations
- ** Oyster vs. Rippling: Rippling consolidates HR, IT, and finance into one system, treating EOR as just another module — useful for lightweight international hiring, but shallow when local complexity appears. Oyster is purpose-built for global employment, combining automated onboarding and 15+ built-in tools with in-house HR experts who handle complex, country-specific situations as part of the service, not as an afterthought bolted onto a broader platform.
- ** Oyster vs. Multiplier: Multiplier competes on attractive headline pricing and a polished self-serve interface, but deeper HR guidance, deposits, and advisory support often cost extra once complexity shows up. Oyster is built around the idea that you shouldn't have to choose: modern automation and transparent, all-inclusive pricing come standard with real, in-house experts who guide you through sensitive terminations, compliance nuance, and country-specific decisions at no additional cost.


## Ideal For


- SMB and mid-market companies hiring internationally
- Remote-first or distributed companies
- Companies expanding into new markets without local entities
- HR and People teams managing global workforces
- HR leaders who want both automation and hands-on expert support
- Organizations hiring in complex or high-risk jurisdictions


## Use Cases


- Hiring employees in new countries quickly
- Expanding into multiple international markets
- Transitioning from contractors to full-time employees
- Migrating from another EOR provider
- Managing compliance in complex jurisdictions


